### Nature Runner — REST Client scratch file
### Install "REST Client" extension in VS Code to run these.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/v1
@token = paste-token-here

### Health
GET {{baseUrl}}

### Sign up a new user
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Thomas Napolitano",
    "username": "thomas",
    "email": "thomas@example.com",
    "password": "secret123",
    "icon": "🏃"
}

### Log in (username or email works for loginId)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "loginId": "thomas",
    "password": "secret123"
}

### Who am I?
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List exercise types (any logged-in user)
GET {{baseUrl}}/exercise-types
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create an activity (user_id is taken from your JWT, not the body)
POST {{baseUrl}}/activities
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "exerciseTypeId": "paste-an-exercise-type-id",
    "title": "Morning Park Jog",
    "description": "A brisk run through the city park",
    "date": "2026-04-23",
    "location": "Central Park",
    "durationMinutes": 30,
    "calories": 200,
    "distanceMiles": 3
}

### List my activities
GET {{baseUrl}}/activities
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Feed (own + accepted friends')
GET {{baseUrl}}/activities/feed
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Stats
GET {{baseUrl}}/activities/stats?period=week
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Search users
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/search?q=thom
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Send friend request
POST {{baseUrl}}/friends/request/paste-other-user-id
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### My friends
GET {{baseUrl}}/friends
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### My incoming friend requests
GET {{baseUrl}}/friends/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Admin: list all users (only works if your JWT is for an admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
